jobs.description:
As a Logistics Employee, you will be part of a team that keeps warehouse operations running smoothly. Depending on your experience and interests, you can work in different departments.

🔧 Tools Department

In the Tools department, you work with specialized equipment and materials.

Your tasks may include:

- Checking tools and materials;
- Scanning products into the system;
- Managing stock levels;
- Preparing materials for shipment;
- Maintaining an organized workspace.

📥 Inbound Department

As an Inbound Employee, you process incoming goods and make sure everything is stored correctly.

Your responsibilities include:

- Receiving deliveries;
- Checking products and quantities;
- Scanning goods into the system;
- Storing products in the correct warehouse locations.

📦 Outbound Department

In Outbound, you make sure customer orders are ready to leave the warehouse.

Your tasks include:

- Picking orders;
- Checking products;
- Packing shipments;
- Preparing orders for transport.

🚜 Reach Truck Positions

Do you have reach truck experience or would you like to develop these skills?

As a Reach Truck Operator, you will:

- Move products throughout the warehouse;
- Replenish stock;
- Pick orders from warehouse racks;
- Work safely at height.

Don't have a certificate yet? Olympia can help you obtain one.

- You are available to work in a 2-shift schedule;
- You speak English, Dutch, or Polish;
- You are motivated and reliable;
- You enjoy working in a team;
- Warehouse experience is a plus, but not required.

Are you looking for a job at a manufacturing company with varied responsibilities? This is a position as an operator working in a 5-shift rotation in the packaging department. In this role, you’ll work as a production worker in a 5-shift rotation at a company in Ittervoort. Your daily tasks will include:

- Operating the (packaging) machine and troubleshooting malfunctions during the packaging process;
- Operating the mixer, where raw materials are blended;
- Working in accordance with HACCP guidelines to ensure food safety;
- Restocking products using a forklift.

You will work in a 5-shift rotation, with the following schedules: 1:45 p.m. – 10:15 p.m., 9:45 p.m. – 6:15 a.m., 5:45 a.m. – 2:15 p.m. (8,5 hours per day).

You can work in various roles, including loader, mixer, filler, and packer. You’ll learn all of this on the job. 

- MBO-level work and thinking skills, preferably in the field of food or engineering. Do you happen to have experience in the food industry? Then you have an edge!;
- Experience operating machinery;
- You are fluent in Dutch or English for safety regulations;
- You have an eye for detail, and you’re also flexible and able to handle stress.

Do you have a forklift certification? That’s a definite plus!

As an operator, you'll work in a two-shift system and be responsible for part of the production process. By operating the machines, your goal is to meet production demand with the desired quality. Independently operate, monitor, and maintain the production line;

- Identify and resolve machine malfunctions;
- Set up machines based on the production schedule;
- Monitor product quality using various measuring instruments;
- Ensure timely machine maintenance in consultation with your manager and the Technical Department;
- Contribute to structural improvement opportunities;
- Coordinating workflows in consultation with your manager.

- A technical background or extensive experience in production technology is a plus;
- You are willing to work night shifts;
- You have technical knowledge and enjoy brainstorming;
- You are a natural at solution-oriented error analysis;
- You are a precision engineer;
- You have knowledge of and experience with production processes;
- You are decisive, practical, and enjoy working in a team.
- A driving license (car) is preferred - Maintec arranges transport;
- You can communicate in English at a B1/B2 level.
